"""
Resolution Studio — desktop launcher.

This is a thin native wrapper: it decodes the bundled copy of the app
(HTML/CSS/JS, the same file that runs inside the browser/Claude version),
writes it to a stable per-user data location, and opens it in a native
webview via pywebview — WKWebView on macOS, WebView2 (Edge/Chromium) on
Windows. No bundled Chromium, no Electron — this rides on whichever
modern webview engine already ships with the OS, so it stays small.

This same file builds on both platforms; just run PyInstaller on the
target OS itself (PyInstaller cannot cross-compile between them):

  macOS:
    pyinstaller --windowed --name "Resolution Studio" --icon=icon.icns app.py
    -> dist/Resolution Studio.app

  Windows (run on an actual Windows machine, or a Windows CI runner):
    pyinstaller --windowed --name "Resolution Studio" --icon=icon.ico app.py
    -> dist\\Resolution Studio\\Resolution Studio.exe
"""

